<title>USA: MBIA qualifies eight muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies eight muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp said Thursday it qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Regional School District No 10, Conn., $4.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Methuen, Mass., $27.96 million municipal purpose loan.</p>
<p>--Bay County Building Authority, Mich., $1.2 million bonds.  </p>
<p>--Livingston County, Mich., $3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Stafford Township, N.J., $8.28 million improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Lexington County School District No 1, S.C., $6 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Austin, Texas, $42.305 million improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Heath, Texas, $1.9 million tax and revenue certificates.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
